# Jon 2026-10-13: the repo carries only what the site needs to build and run.
# Docs, handoffs, editor settings and the blog-restoration working files stay
# on disk but never get pushed. Blog posts (src/content/blog/*.md) are site
# content and stay tracked. The leading slash on /*.md matters: it means the
# repo root only, so it can never catch a blog post.
/*.md
docs/
_restore/
/scripts/
.vscode/
.claude/
Claude outputs/

# _restore/ also holds the WordPress dump: 2 password hashes, 543 email
# addresses, Gravity Forms entries and sent-mail records. Never force-add it.
_restore/*.sql
